---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Legal & attributions"
  description="Ownership, licensing and attribution information for this portfolio and the work it documents."
  updated="2026-09-01"
>
  <h2>Copyright and source license</h2>
  <p>
    Unless otherwise credited, original written content, photographs, artwork
    and portfolio materials on this site are copyright &copy;{' '}
    {site.copyrightStartYear}&ndash;{new Date().getFullYear()} Patrick Barnhardt.
  </p>
  <p>
    Software source code originally authored for this site is available under{' '}
    the <a href="https://github.com/crimsonstrife/crimsonstrife.github.io/blob/master/LICENSE.MD" rel="noopener">MIT License</a>.
    That software license does not grant rights to portfolio copy, photographs,
    artwork, video, project media, personal likeness, trademarks, trade names,
    logos or other brand assets unless a file expressly says otherwise.
    Third-party materials retain their respective rights and licenses.
  </p>

  <h2>Names and brand identities</h2>
  <p>
    CrimsonStrife&trade; and CrimsonStrife Games&trade; are marks used by Patrick
    Barnhardt. Helical Games and STREAMHA&Uuml;S are original legacy names and
    brand identities created by Patrick Barnhardt. The Patrick Barnhardt
    wordmark and monogram, together with the associated original logos and
    visual identities, are brand assets of Patrick Barnhardt.
  </p>

  <h2><cite>One Man's Poison</cite></h2>
  <p>
    The <cite>One Man's Poison</cite> game uses the title and certain characters
    originating in the short film <cite>One Man's Poison</cite>, created by
    James Cotton through Wolf359 Productions, with permission. Rights in the
    original short film and its characters remain with James Cotton and
    Wolf359 Productions. Original game-specific code, systems, writing,
    artwork and other material are owned by or credited to their respective
    creators.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party properties</h2>
  <p>
    Portfolio work may identify, depict or comment on third-party companies,
    products, games and characters. Their names, trademarks, logos and
    underlying creative properties remain with their respective owners. Their
    appearance here is for identification, commentary and portfolio
    documentation and does not imply affiliation, sponsorship or endorsement.
  </p>
  <p>
    Project-specific credits appear alongside the relevant work. Where a
    project adapts an existing character or property, the portfolio may own or
    document the newly created model, texture, code or presentation without
    claiming ownership of the underlying character or property.
  </p>

  <h2>Open-source and design resources</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Font Awesome 6 Free icons are provided by Fonticons, Inc. through Iconify
      and are licensed under{' '}
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="noopener">CC BY 4.0</a>.
      Brand icons are trademarks of their respective owners.
    </li>
    <li>
      Montserrat, Raleway and Roboto are used under the{' '}
      <a href="https://openfontlicense.org/" rel="noopener">SIL Open Font License 1.1</a>.
      Copyright remains with their respective project authors.
    </li>
    <li>
      Other open-source dependencies retain the copyright notices and license
      terms distributed with their source packages.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Questions or corrections</h2>
  <p>
    For a rights question, attribution correction or request concerning
    material on this site, email{' '}<a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
